            "text": "{\"findings\":[{\"tipo\":\"GC\",\"causa_raiz\":\"Alocacao massiva de memoria gerenciada no frame 170 (5.15 MB gerados), desencadeando uma coleta do Garbage Collector que travou a CPU por 22.75 ms. Isso normalmente e causado por instanciacao constante de objetos (Instantiate/new), uso de LINQ em loops de Update, concatenacao excessiva de strings ou criacao de arrays/listas temporarias sem reuso de buffers.\",\"codigo_refatorado\":\"using UnityEngine;\\\\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\\\\n\\\\npublic class NonAllocBufferManager : MonoBehaviour\\\\n{\\\\n    [SerializeField] private GameObject prefabToSpawn;\\\\n    private readonly Queue\u003cGameObject\u003e pool = new Queue\u003cGameObject\u003e();\\\\n    private readonly Collider[] hitBuffer = new Collider[64];\\\\n    private readonly List\u003cint\u003e cachedIntList = new List\u003cint\u003e(1024);\\\\n\\\\n    private void Awake()\\\\n    {\\\\n        for (int i = 0; i \u003c 30; i++)\\\\n        {\\\\n            GameObject obj = Instantiate(prefabToSpawn);\\\\n            obj.SetActive(false);\\\\n            pool.Enqueue(obj);\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    public GameObject GetFromPool(Vector3 position, Quaternion rotation)\\\\n    {\\\\n        GameObject obj = pool.Count \u003e 0 ? pool.Dequeue() : Instantiate(prefabToSpawn);\\\\n        obj.transform.SetPositionAndRotation(position, rotation);\\\\n        obj.SetActive(true);\\\\n        return obj-\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    public void ReturnToPool(GameObject obj)\\\\n    {\\\\n        obj.SetActive(false);\\\\n        pool.Enqueue(obj);\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    private void Update()\\\\n    {\\\\n        int hitCount = Physics.OverlapSphereNonAlloc(transform.position, 10f, hitBuffer);\\\\n        cachedIntList.Clear();\\\\n        for (int i = 0; i \u003c hitCount; i++)\\\\n        {\\\\n            cachedIntList.Add(hitBuffer[i].GetInstanceID());\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n}\",\"explicacao_didatica\":\"O Garbage Collector (coletor de lixo) da Unity e como um caminhao de lixo que precisa parar o transito (o seu jogo) para recolher tudo o que foi descartado. Quando criamos objetos temporarios a cada frame usando 'new', geramos lixo na memoria RAM. Quando a memoria enche, o jogo congela por alguns milissegundos para limpar a sujeira. A solucao e reutilizar os mesmos objetos e listas (tecnica chamada Object Pooling e buffers estaticos), zerando o lixo gerado por frame e eliminando os engasgos.\"}],\"dicas_level_design\":null}",
